To display a matrix as a bitmap with zoom feature in Qt, you can use the QMatrix class for matrix operations and the QImage class for storing and manipulating images. Here's a step-by-step guide:

1. Create a QMatrix object and initialize it with your matrix data.
2. Create a QImage object and set its size based on the matrix dimensions.
3. Loop through each element of the matrix and set the corresponding pixel in the QImage using the QRgb color specifier.
4. Implement a zoom function that scales the QImage by a specified factor. You can use the QTransform class to perform the scaling.
5. Display the QImage in a QWidget using the QPainter class.
6. Add zoom functionality to your application by allowing the user to zoom in and out using mouse scroll or keyboard controls.

Here's some sample code to get you started:
```cpp
#include <QApplication>
#include <QMatrix>
#include <QImage>
#include <QPainter>
#include <QTransform>
#include <QWidget>

int main(int argc, char *argv[])
{
    QApplication app(argc, argv);

    QMatrix matrix;
    // Initialize matrix data here

    QImage image(matrix.rows(), matrix.cols(), QImage::Format_RGB32);
    image.fill(Qt::white);

