2. In your Terraform configuration file (e.g., `main.tf`), add the following code to call the PowerShell script using the `local-exec` provisioner:

```hcl
locals {
  input = "Hello, World!"
}

resource "null_resource" "read_host" {
  triggers = {
    always = "${timestamp()}"
  }

  connection {
    type        = "ssh"
    user        = "your_username"
    private_key = "${file("~/.ssh/your_private_key")}"
    host        = "your_server_ip"
  }

  provisioner "local-exec" {
    command = "powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ./read_host.ps1"
    arguments = ["${local.input}"]
  }
}
```

Replace `your_username`, `your_private_key`, and `your_server_ip` with the appropriate values for your environment.

3. Run `terraform apply` to execute the PowerShell script and prompt for input. The output of the script will be displayed in the Terraform output.

